```
  ═══ LLD — HashMap Resize Corruption Mechanism ═══

  Java 7 transfer() (HEAD insertion — REVERSED!):
  for each entry in old bucket:
    entry.next = newBucket[index];  ← inserts at HEAD
    newBucket[index] = entry;
  // Reverses order! Two threads → circular reference!

  Java 8 resize() (TAIL insertion — no reversal):
  for each entry in old bucket:
    if (hash & oldCapacity == 0) → stays (lo chain)
    else → moves (hi chain)
  // No reversal → no infinite loop!
  // BUT: concurrent modification → lost nodes, wrong trees!

  ConcurrentHashMap resize (Java 8):
  - transferIndex: AtomicInteger tracking progress
  - Each thread claims a STRIDE of buckets
  - synchronized per-bucket during transfer
  - ForwardingNode marks transferred buckets
  - get() during resize: follows ForwardingNode to new table!
  → SAFE concurrent resize!
```
